#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183952 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86cc32d1-5444-5deb-9168-ba67cd8d0e69" :knowledge-point/title "Quadratic Functions Containing an Isolated Perfect Square"}] :question/id #uuid "af43cc58-820d-5f4c-9ab8-e3a8c05bcee0" :question/math-academy-id "e-14873" :question/problem "What is the inverse of $f(x) = (x+4)^2 -3$ for $x\\geq -4?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny = (x+4)^2 -3\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx = (y+4)^2 -3\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =(y+4)^{2}-3 \\\\ x+3 & =(y+4)^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{x+3} & =y+4 \\\\ \\sqrt{x+3}-4 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the positive square root because if $x \\geq -4$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is $f^{-1} \\geq -4.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with $f^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\nf^{-1}(x) = \\sqrt{x + 3} - 4\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183953 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50718b79-529c-5515-bfa2-dbb8b97f4a4a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse by Completing the Square"}] :question/id #uuid "28859a1c-7f0d-58f2-8c77-ff4e27cf610d" :question/math-academy-id "e-14877" :question/problem "What is the inverse of $f(x) = -x^2 + 2x + 6$ for $x\\geq 1?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-{x}^{2}+2x+6 \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}-2x)+6 \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}-2\\cdot x+{1}^{2}-{1}^{2})+6 \\\\  & =-((x-1)^{2}-1)+6 \\\\  & =-(x-1)^{2}+1+6 \\\\  & =-(x-1)^{2}+7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y.$\n\n$$\ny =  -(x-1)^2+ 7\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y.$\n\n$$\nx = -(y-1)^2+ 7\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-(y-1)^{2}+7 \\\\ x-7 & =-(y-1)^{2} \\\\ 7-x & =(y-1)^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{7-x} & =y-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{7-x}+1 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if the domain of $f(x)$ is $x \\geq 1,$ then the range of $f^{-1}(x)$ is  $f^{-1} \\geq 1.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with $f^{-1}(x).$\n\n$$\nf^{-1}(x) = \\sqrt{7-x } +1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183954 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "02655639-b390-510d-9eda-3221375e7e5e" :knowledge-point/title "The Negative Square Root Case"}] :question/id #uuid "836ac184-e55d-5c32-a4af-8a0da847a423" :question/math-academy-id "e-14879" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x) = (x - 3)^2 - 2$ for $x \\leq 3.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y{:}$\n\n$$\ny = (x-3)^2 - 2\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y{:}$\n\n$$\nx = (y - 3)^2 - 2\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =(y-3)^{2}-2 \\\\ x+2 & =(y-3)^{2} \\\\ -\\sqrt{x+2} & =y-3 \\\\ 3-\\sqrt{x+2} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the negative square root because if $x \\leq 3$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is $f^{-1} \\leq 3.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with $f^{-1}(x){:}$\n\n$$\nf^{-1}(x) = 3 - \\sqrt{x + 2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542211 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "02655639-b390-510d-9eda-3221375e7e5e" :knowledge-point/title "The Negative Square Root Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03cf7094-705b-527c-ad76-5e9449f35f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=-4\\sqrt{x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541432} {:answer/id #uuid "3cfe95ee-cc2f-5e90-83e3-8e62d3ddb075" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=-\\sqrt{\\frac{1-x}{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541552} {:answer/id #uuid "b2f041b4-1a2a-5096-8ebb-fab057bff334" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-x}{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541790} {:answer/id #uuid "bbea5fca-afe9-54e8-82aa-eb1cec568d50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=4\\sqrt{1-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541814} {:answer/id #uuid "fd0db8b9-83aa-5b9a-81eb-6de742e59cbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=-\\sqrt{\\frac{x-1}{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cfe95ee-cc2f-5e90-83e3-8e62d3ddb075" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=-\\sqrt{\\frac{1-x}{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541552} :answer-field/id #uuid "78df0292-7df7-57fa-a21d-37fdb23340c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542023}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d281164a-5064-5f5c-ac1f-851a58f31d90" :question/math-academy-id "q-143049" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=1-4{x}^{2}$ for $x\\le 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=1-4{x}^{2}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\nx=1-4{y}^{2}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =1-4{y}^{2} \\\\ x-1 & =-4{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1-x}{4} & ={y}^{2} \\\\ -\\sqrt{\\frac{1-x}{4}} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the negative square root because if $x\\le 0$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\le 0.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=-\\sqrt{\\frac{1-x}{4}}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542194 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "02655639-b390-510d-9eda-3221375e7e5e" :knowledge-point/title "The Negative Square Root Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06eeaff7-edf7-5210-a272-a01667cc7853" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=3\\sqrt{1-x}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541435} {:answer/id #uuid "6626f619-b878-5819-baf0-cde23eedb181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=2+\\sqrt{\\frac{x-1}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541631} {:answer/id #uuid "73f79f59-a66f-50cb-8b41-2190e2c051bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=-3\\sqrt{x-3}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541659} {:answer/id #uuid "e4f03874-1af5-5cf6-8ad1-b18a91ce6411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=2-\\sqrt{\\frac{x-1}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541907} {:answer/id #uuid "e8fcc335-23c3-5aa9-bfaf-1b52de7212de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=-2-\\sqrt{\\frac{1-x}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4f03874-1af5-5cf6-8ad1-b18a91ce6411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=2-\\sqrt{\\frac{x-1}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541907} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9aca599-1b05-506b-80c8-6fbc19e4fd06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542102}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b5d4ec46-41de-5071-92d0-61a853c21e80" :question/math-academy-id "q-143057" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-12x+13$ for $x\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =3{x}^{2}-12x+13 \\\\  & =3({x}^{2}-4x)+13 \\\\  & =3({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x)+13 \\\\  & =3({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2}-{2}^{2})+13 \\\\  & =3((x-2)^{2}-4)+13 \\\\  & =3(x-2)^{2}-12+13 \\\\  & =3(x-2)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nTo find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=3(x-2)^{2}+1\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\nx=3(y-2)^{2}+1\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3(y-2)^{2}+1 \\\\ 3(y-2)^{2} & =x-1 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =\\frac{x-1}{3} \\\\ y-2 & =-\\sqrt{\\frac{x-1}{3}} \\\\ y & =2-\\sqrt{\\frac{x-1}{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the negative square root because if the domain of $f(x)$ is $x\\le 2,$ then the range of ${f}^{-1}(x)$ is  ${f}^{-1}\\le 2.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=2-\\sqrt{\\frac{x-1}{3}}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542167 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86cc32d1-5444-5deb-9168-ba67cd8d0e69" :knowledge-point/title "Quadratic Functions Containing an Isolated Perfect Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f75e124-e436-5cb6-a6ea-00c0d01cc770" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{3-x}{8}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541712} {:answer/id #uuid "93add3cb-2391-549e-b878-727d8ced375e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{8-x}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541727} {:answer/id #uuid "ab4089ca-1521-5cb3-bf59-51753beac06d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{8+x}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541777} {:answer/id #uuid "afdb4a83-577b-5ef0-a83b-f197fc089382" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{8-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541784} {:answer/id #uuid "f288f1fe-4411-5664-a14e-8335888b1182" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{x-8}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93add3cb-2391-549e-b878-727d8ced375e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{8-x}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541727} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfc62a3b-f558-5854-ac8e-70f82cd6d2d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542064}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8ea93b33-07b4-5d80-ad03-66a9bad29401" :question/math-academy-id "q-143069" :question/problem "What is the inverse of $f(x)=8-3{x}^{2}$ for $x\\ge 0?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=8-3{x}^{2}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=8-3{y}^{2}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =8-3{y}^{2} \\\\ x-8 & =-3{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{8-x}{3} & ={y}^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{8-x}{3}} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge 0$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge 0.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{8-x}{3}}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542218 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50718b79-529c-5515-bfa2-dbb8b97f4a4a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse by Completing the Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4319b2c4-39ec-5c51-aa83-72ddce82c325" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x+8}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541563} {:answer/id #uuid "62d8d287-27b6-54ec-9924-e2769ce58323" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x+2}-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541627} {:answer/id #uuid "89cf21be-fb2d-54b9-be60-4dd3118b8c0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x+8}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541700} {:answer/id #uuid "9766ce90-e2b5-5ef2-904a-42eedf996b1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x-8}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541738} {:answer/id #uuid "b6bfdd3f-e14a-5038-acb8-0a79fa5ed9ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x-2}+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541798}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4319b2c4-39ec-5c51-aa83-72ddce82c325" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x+8}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541563} :answer-field/id #uuid "0780126b-332c-53d9-b934-635577e9364a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541966}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eaa3b305-adcb-5660-ac47-ef5d46e7e553" :question/math-academy-id "q-143083" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)={x}^{2}+4x-4$ for $x\\ge -2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{2}+4x-4 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})-{2}^{2}-4 \\\\  & =(x+2)^{2}-4-4 \\\\  & =(x+2)^{2}-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nTo find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=(x+2)^{2}-8\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=(y+2)^{2}-8\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =(y+2)^{2}-8 \\\\ x+8 & =(y+2)^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{x+8} & =y+2 \\\\ \\sqrt{x+8}-2 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge -2$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge -2.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x+8}-2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50718b79-529c-5515-bfa2-dbb8b97f4a4a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse by Completing the Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01adf5ca-64db-5382-bf4e-1ca6626f2017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{x+5}{2}}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541428} {:answer/id #uuid "3610cb6e-1d88-5270-9eb9-3fc955a303b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{x+5}{2}}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541534} {:answer/id #uuid "5700f3c9-9e4a-59b7-82bd-d9f02926b4ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{x+1}{2}}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541594} {:answer/id #uuid "6f3956b9-f9d3-5785-8264-d835a400bc7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{x-1}{2}}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541646} {:answer/id #uuid "745b1685-5eb1-51ee-9435-82fa42898591" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{x-5}{2}}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "745b1685-5eb1-51ee-9435-82fa42898591" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{x-5}{2}}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541660} :answer-field/id #uuid "0de6a724-f7f8-5dd1-a8c0-8827537e07fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541969}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2079d901-07f2-590c-b43f-09625015f43f" :question/math-academy-id "q-143084" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=2{x}^{2}-4x+7$ for $x\\ge 1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =2{x}^{2}-4x+7 \\\\  & =2({x}^{2}-2x)+7 \\\\  & =2({x}^{2}-2\\cdot x+{1}^{2}-{1}^{2})+7 \\\\  & =2((x-1)^{2}-1)+7 \\\\  & =2(x-1)^{2}-2+7 \\\\  & =2(x-1)^{2}+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nTo find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=2(x-1)^{2}+5\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=2(y-1)^{2}+5\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2(y-1)^{2}+5 \\\\ x-5 & =2(y-1)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{x-5}{2} & =(y-1)^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{x-5}{2}} & =y-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{x-5}{2}}+1 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge 1$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge 1.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{x-5}{2}}+1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86cc32d1-5444-5deb-9168-ba67cd8d0e69" :knowledge-point/title "Quadratic Functions Containing an Isolated Perfect Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b715b42-b0b1-5a40-842f-6f587c2d8a6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7-x}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b715b42-b0b1-5a40-842f-6f587c2d8a6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7-x}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541509} :answer-field/id #uuid "24c26333-1433-5c1e-991d-f29fb85f24d4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f9b3665f-1e6e-5b22-b4a7-a783bccbb796" :question/math-academy-id "q-222050" :question/problem "What is the inverse of $f(x)=7-(x+1)^{2}$ for $x\\ge -1?$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=7-(x+1)^{2}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=7-(y+1)^{2}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =7-(y+1)^{2} \\\\ x-7 & =-(y+1)^{2} \\\\ 7-x & =(y+1)^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{7-x} & =y+1 \\\\ \\sqrt{7-x}-1 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the positive square root because if $x\\ge -1$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge -1.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{7-x}-1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542162 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50718b79-529c-5515-bfa2-dbb8b97f4a4a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse by Completing the Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10c2a310-044a-5f3c-bb71-f5d989b6904f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{x+85}}{2}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541456}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10c2a310-044a-5f3c-bb71-f5d989b6904f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{x+85}}{2}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541456} :answer-field/id #uuid "3946464e-1cb3-5c3e-bb8c-2f2bf6ad8794" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541995}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "79783b94-bb53-5240-8c0c-52c93a581d6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-222054" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=4{x}^{2}-40x+15$ for $x\\ge 5.$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =4{x}^{2}-40x+15 \\\\  & =4({x}^{2}-10x)+15 \\\\  & =4({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 5x+{5}^{2}-{5}^{2})+15 \\\\  & =4((x-5)^{2}-25)+15 \\\\  & =4(x-5)^{2}-100+15 \\\\  & =4(x-5)^{2}-85\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nTo find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=4(x-5)^{2}-85\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=4(y-5)^{2}-85\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4(y-5)^{2}-85 \\\\ x+85 & =4(y-5)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{x+85}{4} & =(y-5)^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{x+85}{4}} & =y-5 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{x+85}}{2}+5 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge 5$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge 5.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{\\sqrt{x+85}}{2}+5\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542199 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50718b79-529c-5515-bfa2-dbb8b97f4a4a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse by Completing the Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3e618a1-af10-5010-9e87-ba571f9eac66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{x-4}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3e618a1-af10-5010-9e87-ba571f9eac66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{x-4}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541792} :answer-field/id #uuid "9dcd2080-a93e-5b4c-a8e3-757eef234fed" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542042}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b957784b-0ac4-5ba4-bc18-3ca9998ce9ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-222055" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)={x}^{2}-12x+40$ for $x\\ge 6.$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{2}-12x+40 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 6x+{6}^{2})-{6}^{2}+40 \\\\  & =(x-6)^{2}-36+40 \\\\  & =(x-6)^{2}+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nTo find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=(x-6)^{2}+4\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=(y-6)^{2}+4\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =(y-6)^{2}+4 \\\\ x-4 & =(y-6)^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{x-4} & =y-6 \\\\ \\sqrt{x-4}+6 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge 6$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge 6.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x-4}+6\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542224 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "02655639-b390-510d-9eda-3221375e7e5e" :knowledge-point/title "The Negative Square Root Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bab48d8a-b265-55bb-854c-211daf398ed6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{\\frac{-x-1}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bab48d8a-b265-55bb-854c-211daf398ed6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{\\frac{-x-1}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541807} :answer-field/id #uuid "d227cfa7-f5ea-5316-99fc-720e33bb25d4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "effbd8f4-b559-5948-841a-8a16bd6f2c1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-222063" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=-3{x}^{2}-1$ for $x\\le 0.$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=-3{x}^{2}-1\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\nx=-3{y}^{2}-1\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-3{y}^{2}-1 \\\\ x+1 & =-3{y}^{2} \\\\ -\\frac{x+1}{3} & ={y}^{2} \\\\ -\\sqrt{-\\frac{x+1}{3}} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the negative square root because if $x\\le 0$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\le 0.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=-\\sqrt{-\\frac{x+1}{3}}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542121 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "02655639-b390-510d-9eda-3221375e7e5e" :knowledge-point/title "The Negative Square Root Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "044e0814-a8c1-5806-b474-59af79f033a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\sqrt{\\frac{13-x}{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "044e0814-a8c1-5806-b474-59af79f033a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\sqrt{\\frac{13-x}{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541434} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6d97c62-1d5e-5227-b2ef-a71a4c4a2269" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1749af1b-7a2a-52a7-adf9-0527962ea5b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-222071" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=-10{x}^{2}+40x-27$ for $x\\le 2.$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-10{x}^{2}+40x-27 \\\\  & =-10({x}^{2}-4x)-27 \\\\  & =-10(({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})-{2}^{2})-27 \\\\  & =-10((x-2)^{2}-4)-27 \\\\  & =-10{(x-2)}^{2}+40-27 \\\\  & =-10{(x-2)}^{2}+13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nTo find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=-10{(x-2)}^{2}+13\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\nx=-10{(y-2)}^{2}+13\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-10{(y-2)}^{2}+13 \\\\ 10{(y-2)}^{2} & =13-x \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =\\frac{13-x}{10} \\\\ y-2 & =-\\sqrt{\\frac{13-x}{10}} \\\\ y & =2-\\sqrt{\\frac{13-x}{10}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the negative square root because if the domain of $f(x)$ is $x\\le 2,$ then the range of ${f}^{-1}(x)$ is  ${f}^{-1}\\le 2.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=2-\\sqrt{\\frac{13-x}{10}}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184789 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "02655639-b390-510d-9eda-3221375e7e5e" :knowledge-point/title "The Negative Square Root Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fd6c04e-bd57-55da-add3-cea4ec07223c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x-7}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541454} {:answer/id #uuid "2745c2c9-cedc-58f3-915e-77275bb543c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=-\\sqrt{x-7}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541502} {:answer/id #uuid "78226fa3-0be1-5dbb-a1b5-44e766cce3a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=-\\sqrt{x+7}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541670} {:answer/id #uuid "8dc54b87-c7b6-58a2-9f97-7d4d599e1fc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=-\\sqrt{x+1}-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541708} {:answer/id #uuid "af69e7a7-55e9-5173-9778-c68468170160" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x+1}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541782}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2745c2c9-cedc-58f3-915e-77275bb543c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=-\\sqrt{x-7}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541502} :answer-field/id #uuid "3748a2b3-6e6e-58cf-b9a7-b382cfce2fe2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183343}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e2e323d3-460f-5bcb-be71-a754f4dd2852" :question/math-academy-id "q-46347" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=(x+1)^{2}+7$ for $x\\le -1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=(x+1)^{2}+7\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=(y+1)^{2}+7\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =(y+1)^{2}+7 \\\\ x-7 & =(y+1)^{2} \\\\ -\\sqrt{x-7} & =y+1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{x-7}-1 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the negative square root because if $x\\le -1$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\le -1.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=-\\sqrt{x-7}-1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184790 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86cc32d1-5444-5deb-9168-ba67cd8d0e69" :knowledge-point/title "Quadratic Functions Containing an Isolated Perfect Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f25b658-da99-5358-809a-4ca741fcc3ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541486} {:answer/id #uuid "2aa580a4-0250-5334-9f19-69eb1e224f54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541507} {:answer/id #uuid "5f85716e-b895-57c4-a078-5da001aec196" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x-16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541613} {:answer/id #uuid "75a38130-7e1c-5938-8730-ba5bd2e0cb78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541665} {:answer/id #uuid "f7a432a2-7c85-5d88-968b-291cd238a4bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x+4}+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2aa580a4-0250-5334-9f19-69eb1e224f54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541507} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9676208-780b-5083-930f-6b64501598cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183349}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5a86ad5d-8d37-5ba1-8cda-db2245e4944e" :question/math-academy-id "q-46393" :question/problem "What is the inverse of $f(x)={x}^{2}-16$ for $x\\ge 0?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}-16\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx={y}^{2}-16\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={y}^{2}-16 \\\\ x+16 & ={y}^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{x+16} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge 0$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge 0.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x+16}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542117 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86cc32d1-5444-5deb-9168-ba67cd8d0e69" :knowledge-point/title "Quadratic Functions Containing an Isolated Perfect Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14725012-8996-52a9-836d-06f6e288f17b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541463} {:answer/id #uuid "5e4cfd10-bb53-5d8d-99b8-2535e0b1a6bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{x+6}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541612} {:answer/id #uuid "60664750-a517-511e-b4f4-cfc49f8eda5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{\\sqrt{x-6}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541618} {:answer/id #uuid "7a3d0aff-5f29-530d-a3d1-0883a12a9aba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541673} {:answer/id #uuid "ca59039a-3841-5c41-8f1c-20fa5dddb820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{\\sqrt{x+6}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e4cfd10-bb53-5d8d-99b8-2535e0b1a6bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{x+6}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541612} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7b40f01-a4ff-5098-a182-9517ac54d555" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "10ace3a5-6164-50ba-ba18-c598288b7099" :question/math-academy-id "q-46395" :question/problem "What is the inverse of $f(x)=2{x}^{2}-6$ for $x\\ge 0?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=2{x}^{2}-6\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=2{y}^{2}-6\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{y}^{2}-6 \\\\ x+6 & =2{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{x+6}{2} & ={y}^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{x+6}{2}} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge 0$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge 0.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{x+6}{2}}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542111 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86cc32d1-5444-5deb-9168-ba67cd8d0e69" :knowledge-point/title "Quadratic Functions Containing an Isolated Perfect Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a4e80b0-35b3-5e58-9f28-a3996499979e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{\\sqrt{5-x}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541475} {:answer/id #uuid "96124387-7e0e-56c3-b953-fbc033f59488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{\\sqrt{x-5}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541733} {:answer/id #uuid "9ec756fa-d499-5629-8976-7cd77dd49efc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=-\\sqrt{\\frac{x-5}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541753} {:answer/id #uuid "e21389f9-a670-5fa3-8a76-e5f18542afa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{\\sqrt{5-x}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541901} {:answer/id #uuid "f8ff4676-0f75-5568-84be-c3e33b6f9d92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{\\sqrt{x+5}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a4e80b0-35b3-5e58-9f28-a3996499979e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{\\sqrt{5-x}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541475} :answer-field/id #uuid "8680c355-7f1a-5770-8da2-2ed51afefd72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0439240f-2359-52c3-a019-0d15653653ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-46396" :question/problem "What is the inverse of $f(x)=5-9{x}^{2}$ for $x\\ge 0?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=5-9{x}^{2}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=5-9{y}^{2}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5-9{y}^{2} \\\\ x-5 & =-9{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{5-x}{9} & ={y}^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{5-x}{9}} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge 0$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge 0.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{\\sqrt{5-x}}{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542163 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50718b79-529c-5515-bfa2-dbb8b97f4a4a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse by Completing the Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f019ffc-3f62-52e8-80cb-d42dfa1d06d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{6-x}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541452} {:answer/id #uuid "509957a9-6817-5fc4-b630-b082ad65252f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x-6}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541587} {:answer/id #uuid "84956849-64c9-5ae0-8033-82a3b1313a10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{-x+6}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541691} {:answer/id #uuid "d80f4553-3510-5a33-90a3-4980dad3cdbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{-x-6}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541884} {:answer/id #uuid "e9dca48e-0c58-502e-8643-f8f090002129" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x+6}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84956849-64c9-5ae0-8033-82a3b1313a10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{-x+6}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541691} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd37fde4-7f0f-589d-ab1a-1f5cac19e63d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "87d49f48-029f-525c-b4c7-c630bf956527" :question/math-academy-id "q-46409" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=-{x}^{2}+2x+5$ for $x\\ge 1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-{x}^{2}+2x+5 \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}-2x)+5 \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}-2\\cdot x+{1}^{2}-{1}^{2})+5 \\\\  & =-((x-1)^{2}-1)+5 \\\\  & =-(x-1)^{2}+1+5 \\\\  & =-(x-1)^{2}+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nTo find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=-(x-1)^{2}+6\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=-(y-1)^{2}+6\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-(y-1)^{2}+6 \\\\ x-6 & =-(y-1)^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{-x+6} & =y-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{-x+6}+1 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge 1$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge 1.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{-x+6}+1\n$$"}]}
